    <!--
      The launch window, painted before Compose has a frame. It is the start
      destination's canvas — Logbook `paper`, light here and dark in
      values-night — so the handoff into the real theme is invisible in both.

      It used to be bound specifically to journal's entry in the destination
      table, back when a tab could still be on the other design system and
      painting the wrong one here meant a frame of the wrong page on every cold
      start. With Graphite Signal retired every destination is paper, so this
      value tracks the palette rather than a route. `ShellChromeTest` pins the
      other half: the Scaffold canvas these two colours have to match.
    -->
    <color name="window_background">#FBFAF7</color>
</resources>
